    "body": "## Motivation\nFollow-up to #43006. That PR made the dsv4/dsv32/dsv41 encoders honor `tool_choice=\"none\"` for request-level tools, but the OpenAI protocol also allows `tools` on individual system/developer messages, and those schemas were still rendered into the prompt by the encoders. Since the DSML parser is disabled under `tool_choice=\"none\"`, the model can echo raw DSML markers into `message.content`. This covers the remaining case in #35736.\n\n## Modifications\n- `serving_chat.py`: when `tool_choice == \"none\"`, pop message-level `tools` from the copied messages before encoding. Request-level tools were already gated upstream; the original wire request is left untouched.\n- Regression test covering dsv4/dsv32/dsv41 with a developer message carrying tools, asserting the prompt contains no tool schemas and the original request is unmodified.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nParser-scoped fix; no change to model outputs under default settings.\n\n```\npytest test/registered/unit/entrypoints/openai/test_serving_chat.py -k dsv_tool_choice_none\n# 2 passed (includes the existing #43006 test), 9 subtests passed\n```\n\n## Speed Tests\nNot applicable — prompt-construction change exercised only under `tool_choice=\"none\"`.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] pre-commit hooks pass on the touched files\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39564684683](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39564684683)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39564684732](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39564684732)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39564684607](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39564684607)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
